      "query": "manual adjudication PDF page query",
      "results": [
        {
          "id": "docs/ide/getting-started/best-practices_public.md_chunk_10",
          "score": 5.1096363,
          "content": "Context mentions let you reference specific elements of your project directly in your conversations with Bob:\n\n- Use `@/path/to/file.js` to include specific file contents.\n- Use `@/path/to/folder` to include all files in a directory.\n- Use `@problems` to include Bob Findings panel diagnostics.\n- Use `@terminal` to include recent terminal output.\n- Highlight text and use the keyboard shortcut `⌘` + `L` to add it to the chat.\n- Attach `.docx`, `.pdf`, and `.xlsx` files directly as context without manually extracting their content.\n\nThis approach is more efficient than copying and pasting code or describing file locations.\n\nLearn more about context mentions in the [Context mentions](/docs/ide/features/context-mentions) documentation.",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Best practices \u003e Communication strategies \u003e Use context mentions"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.000019525885
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/ide/features/auto-approving-actions_public.md_chunk_3",
          "score": 0.75178814,
          "content": "When you auto-approve an action, Bob will complete the respective action without asking for permission.\n\n\u003cimg src=\"/images/auto-approve-permissions.png\" alt=\"Auto-approve permissions panel showing available actions\" width=\"300\" /\u003e\n\nThe **Read** action allows you to view your files and directory content and has a Medium risk level.\nThe **Edit** action allows you to create, edit, and save files to your directory and has a **High** risk level.\nThe **Execute** action allows you to run commands in your terminal and has a **High** risk level.\nThe **MCP** action allows you to use MCP servers you have configured and has a Medium-**High** risk level.\nThe **Skill** action allows you to activate skills you have defined and has a Medium risk level.\nThe **Todo** action allows you to update the todo list and has a Low risk level.\nThe **Subtask** action allows you to create and complete subtasks and has a Low risk level.\nThe **Subagent** action allows you to spawn subagents to handle focused tasks and has a Low risk level.\nThe **Mode** action allows you to switch modes to complete a task and has a Low risk level.",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Auto-approve \u003e Available actions"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.000015936621
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/ide/configuration/carbon-modes/images-to-react_public.md_chunk_4",
          "score": 4.954297,
          "content": "To verify that Carbon React mode is working correctly:\n\n1. Type a question about Carbon React components in the chat window, such as:\n   ```\n   What card components does Carbon React support?\n   ```\n2. Bob will query the Carbon MCP, which requires your permission\n3. After processing, Bob will present the results with information about Carbon React card components\n\n![Carbon react prompt and start of response](/images/carbon-react-query.png)\n\n![Carbon react results from Bob - Task Completed](/images/carbon-react-results.png)",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Set up for Images to React \u003e Using Carbon React mode \u003e Verifying the setup"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.000015812602
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/ide/security/security-hardening_public.md_chunk_25",
          "score": 6.515969,
          "content": "- **MUST** hash secrets in logs and error messages\n- **MUST** use secure random generation for tokens (secrets.token_urlsafe())\n- **MUST** use cryptographically secure compare methods\n- **MUST** implement secret expiration and rotation\n- **NEVER** pass secrets in URLs or query parameters\n\n---",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Run application \u003e 4. Secrets and Credential Management \u003e Credential Handling Requirements"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.00001544631
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/ide/security/security-hardening_public.md_chunk_38",
          "score": 0.76033545,
          "content": "- **MUST** validate all user inputs (type, length, format, range)\n- **MUST** sanitize inputs to prevent injection attacks\n- **MUST** use parameterized queries for database operations\n- **MUST** encode outputs based on context (HTML, JavaScript, SQL, URL)\n- **NEVER** trust client-side validation",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Run application \u003e 9. Input Validation and Output Encoding \u003e P0 - Critical Requirements (MUST)"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.00001485458
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

